  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 2 December 2026 at 10:00AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nPositioned just moments from the shoreline and Vellenoweth Green, 12 Auckland Road combines the peace of mind of a comprehensive, renovation and with one of St Heliers' most sought-after coastal addresses.\r\n\r\nReimagined, this 257m² (more of less) freehold residence delivers modern architectural polish without the maintenance of a large section. A brand-new Colorsteel roof, full double glazing, warm timber flooring, and black-framed internal glass doors set a crisp, contemporary tone throughout. At the heart of the home, a sleek timber-and-white designer kitchen anchors generous open-plan living and dining spaces, flowing seamlessly out to elevated balconies capturing sunsets across Vellenoweth Green, St Heliers Bay, and Rangitoto Island.\r\n\r\nThoughtfully configured across three levels for modern family dynamics, the layout includes:\r\n\r\n• Four generous bedrooms and 3.5 bathrooms, offering effortless comfort for family and guests alike.\r\n\r\n• Three separate living zones, giving everyone room to spread out without losing connection.\r\n\r\n• A semi-self-contained lower level, ideal for teenagers, extended family, an au pair, or a private work-from-home suite.\r\n\r\n• Double internal-access garaging plus additional off-street parking, a rare practical advantage this close to the village.\r\n\r\nLeave the car at home and step straight into the St Heliers lifestyle: morning swims at the beach, flat walks across Vellenoweth Green, and beachfront cafes and restaurants just two minutes from your front door, all within zone for St Heliers School, St Ignatius School, and Glendowie College.\r\n\r\nSolid, stylish, and move-in ready, inspect at this week's open homes or contact Paul and Jo to arrange a private viewing ahead of the auction.",
